A||||3||FieroPerformance||How to hook a starter up on the V6?||||1||
Z||000000||FieroPerformance||11-12-2001||09:58 PM||||Alright, my engine is back in the car after a very time consuming rebuild. I am having trouble figuring out which wires go where on the starter. I know that the positive battery cables hooks to the larger terminal, but there are a black and a brown wire (together), and a black and a blue wire (together) that look as though they should hook to the same terminal but when they are all hooked up there is not enough room for the nut that holds them on. I have a red wire to the smaller terminal.<P>Please let me know if you have any idea what I am talking about and what goes where.<P>Thanks,<BR>-Charlie<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsigfperformance.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||11-12-2001||10:19 PM||||Positive big red wire to the large terminal (you got that one, right?) on the starter. One small single wire to the small terminal (I think it's red also) on the starter. The pair of double wires attach to the transmission side of the head closest to the back seat, they are grounds.||||reg||1
Z||000002||tgowens||11-13-2001||01:12 AM||||Charlie, Indiana is right - <I>both</I> of those pairs bolt onto the side of the block with 15mm bolts (I am assuming that they both have the lugs on the ends of them?) -- one pair on each bolt - you should be able to figure out which goes where as one pair will be longer than the other pair....<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_TGO.jpg"> <P><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroPerformance||11-13-2001||03:59 PM||||Thanks a bunch guys. This forum is a really good tool.<P>-Charlie<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsigfperformance.jpg"> ||||reg||1
